# escape_shade_file -- the poet, one of the dead waiting at the well. He died with the last line of a poem missing,
# and keeps saying it over, waiting for the end to come to him. Before Géaga looks away he waits as you do; after, she
# has let you go.

@file underworld/escape
@encounter 11

= the poem
@when !note escape_geaga_blind_eye
Three hazels bend above the pool,
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Three salmon take the falling nut;
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
What the water knows, it will not tell,
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
What the tree knows, it has forgot—
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= she let you go
@when note escape_geaga_blind_eye
She let you go? Then the last line is up there somewhere, under the sky.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
If you hear it, at a fire, from a child, anywhere at all: keep it for me.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
